BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Festival (formerly Halloween in the Hills)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261017T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261017T210000
UID:4060098e2a1d29ab235915fd0514e3a5@wfhb.org
DESCRIPTION:12pm to 4pm: Halloween Arts and Crafts: Stop by the Nature Cen
 ter in the afternoon to do some crafts\, including animal Halloween masks!
  You may stay and use our supplies or take paper to go. 5:30pm to 7pm: Tri
 ck or Treating in the campground. Visit marked participating sites to tric
 k or treat! Participating sites can pick up a sign from the campground gat
 ehouse.  Please stay on foot and do not trick or treat out of cars. 7pm t
 o 9pm: Campfire Stories: Bring a story to read or a tale to tell. Save any
  scary stories for after 8:30pm. Feel free to bring campfire snacks! The P
 umpkin Carving Contest entrees will be on display. Hikes: 7pm to 9pm: Cand
 lelight Hike: Hike the Discovery Trail at the Nature Center. The path will
  be lit by small candles\, but your own flashlight is advised as a backup!
  Wear close-toed shoes or boots\, do not wear sandals or flip flops.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park Nature Center\, 1801 IN-46\, Nashville
URL:https://wfhb.org/events/fall-festival-formerly-halloween-in-the-hills/
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
END:VEVENT
