BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Safety Cabaret by Delong Academy: Rehearsal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261019T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261019T170000
UID:db0665f16a3becf53a2b47c4c2c18ecc@wfhb.org
DESCRIPTION:Rehearsal will focus on how all of those departments come toge
 ther when the performer enters the equation. Using a real technical-rehear
 sal environment\, participants will explore communication between performe
 rs\, stage management\, rigging\, lighting\, audio\, scenic\, and other pr
 oduction personnel. The day creates space for questions that are often dif
 ficult to address during a normal production schedule. What information do
 es lighting need from the performer? What does audio need before rehearsal
  begins? How do scenic or rigging decisions affect blocking? What does sta
 ge management need from each department? How should a performer ask about 
 a technical element they do not understand? How should a technician explai
 n a concern without relying on jargon? These conversations are valuable no
 t only for performers\, but also for technicians. A lighting technician be
 nefits from understanding what the audio department is trying to accomplis
 h. A rigger benefits from understanding how scenic and lighting department
 s use the equipment being supported. Stage management benefits from unders
 tanding where technical bottlenecks occur. Everyone benefits from knowing 
 enough about the other departments to recognize when a decision may have c
 onsequences beyond their own work. Participants may register for individua
 l days or the full three-day event. Registration and additional event info
 rmation: https://delong.ludus.com/show_page.php?show_id=200534364 Safety C
 abaret is a hands-on\, interactive training event designed for people thro
 ughout the live entertainment industry. Rather than separating performers
 \, technicians\, stage managers\, and safety professionals into different 
 classrooms\, the program uses the real process of loading in\, rehearsing
 \, and loading out a production as the learning environment. A major focus
  of the event is cross-department education. Rigging\, lighting\, audio\, 
 carpentry\, stage management\, and other production departments are often 
 highly specialized\, but they depend on one another constantly. Safety Cab
 aret gives technicians the opportunity to learn more about what the other 
 departments do\, why they do it\, what information they need\, and how one
  department’s decisions can affect everyone else in the room.
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood Ave.\,  Bloomington\,  
 IN
URL:https://wfhb.org/events/safety-cabaret-by-delong-academy-rehearsal/
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
END:VEVENT
